[{:db/id "c6454838-da94-524c-851e-653529507ee9" :answer/id #uuid "c6454838-da94-524c-851e-653529507ee9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4 x + y + 2=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1b082478-c820-5762-b2a2-2a62271a3ef2" :answer/id #uuid "1b082478-c820-5762-b2a2-2a62271a3ef2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4 x + y - 2=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d9fe04c2-63a3-5665-902d-743af1759e1a" :answer/id #uuid "d9fe04c2-63a3-5665-902d-743af1759e1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4 x + y=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "982c2d81-f814-5d6a-aa38-881e92050088" :answer/id #uuid "982c2d81-f814-5d6a-aa38-881e92050088" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2 x + y=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ba020276-b69d-5fef-ba06-976da1e22be0" :answer/id #uuid "ba020276-b69d-5fef-ba06-976da1e22be0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x - 4 y - 9=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "af862b75-ced5-50a1-9df7-adc532c40789" :answer-field/id #uuid "af862b75-ced5-50a1-9df7-adc532c40789" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["c6454838-da94-524c-851e-653529507ee9" "1b082478-c820-5762-b2a2-2a62271a3ef2" "d9fe04c2-63a3-5665-902d-743af1759e1a" "982c2d81-f814-5d6a-aa38-881e92050088" "ba020276-b69d-5fef-ba06-976da1e22be0"] :answer-field/correct "1b082478-c820-5762-b2a2-2a62271a3ef2" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "3df1a962-28ed-5ee8-927b-1c62b88a956c" :question/id #uuid "3df1a962-28ed-5ee8-927b-1c62b88a956c" :question/problem "Consider the plane curve $x^{2} + 2 y^{2}=9.$  Find the equation of the normal line to the curve at the point $(1,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "If we set $f(x,y)=x^{2} + 2 y^{2}$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=9.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(1,-2)$ can be found by computing $∇f(1,-2).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(1,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2} + 2 y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{2} + 2 y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(2 x)\\,i+(4 y)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(1,-2) & =(2 (1))\\,i+(4 (-2))\\,j \\\\  & =(2)\\,i+(-8)\\,j \\\\  & =⟨2,-8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(1,-2)=⟨2,-8⟩$ is a normal vector to the curve at $(1,-2).$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}} & =\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}} \\\\ \\frac{x-(1)}{2} & =\\frac{y-(-2)}{-8} \\\\ (-8)(x-(1)) & =(2)(y-(-2)) \\\\ (-4)(x-(1)) & =(1)(y-(-2)) \\\\ 4 - 4 x & =y + 2 \\\\ 4 x + y - 2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["af862b75-ced5-50a1-9df7-adc532c40789"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "6061ce51-b351-522a-bca9-76aa11187e78" :answer/id #uuid "6061ce51-b351-522a-bca9-76aa11187e78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3 x + 2 y + 3=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "884d0d51-859f-5fea-96a9-8818c3c7184f" :answer/id #uuid "884d0d51-859f-5fea-96a9-8818c3c7184f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2 x - 3 y + 11=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1df7a5cf-c5ee-5d5d-bbcf-a92c76ab4ef5" :answer/id #uuid "1df7a5cf-c5ee-5d5d-bbcf-a92c76ab4ef5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3 x + 4 y - 9=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "3be2a23d-ef2c-595f-9cf8-9a45f0a1d019" :answer/id #uuid "3be2a23d-ef2c-595f-9cf8-9a45f0a1d019" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3 x + 2 y - 3=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5b126564-37ea-568a-a5ff-6329c3df1cc4" :answer/id #uuid "5b126564-37ea-568a-a5ff-6329c3df1cc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3 x + 2 y=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a3e69355-4465-5521-9779-bce1af127a1b" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3e69355-4465-5521-9779-bce1af127a1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["6061ce51-b351-522a-bca9-76aa11187e78" "884d0d51-859f-5fea-96a9-8818c3c7184f" "1df7a5cf-c5ee-5d5d-bbcf-a92c76ab4ef5" "3be2a23d-ef2c-595f-9cf8-9a45f0a1d019" "5b126564-37ea-568a-a5ff-6329c3df1cc4"] :answer-field/correct "3be2a23d-ef2c-595f-9cf8-9a45f0a1d019" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "c34c8b85-1410-5a9f-8287-4a3353c69bd2" :question/id #uuid "c34c8b85-1410-5a9f-8287-4a3353c69bd2" :question/problem "Consider the plane curve $4 x^{2} + 2 y^{2}=22.$  Find the equation of the normal line to the curve at the point $(-1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "If we set $f(x,y)=4 x^{2} + 2 y^{2}$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=22.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(-1,3)$ can be found by computing $∇f(-1,3).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(-1,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4 x^{2} + 2 y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4 x^{2} + 2 y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(8 x)\\,i+(4 y)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(-1,3) & =(8 (-1))\\,i+(4 (3))\\,j \\\\  & =(-8)\\,i+(12)\\,j \\\\  & =⟨-8,12⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(-1,3)=⟨-8,12⟩$ is a normal vector to the curve at $(-1,3).$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}} & =\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}} \\\\ \\frac{x-(-1)}{-8} & =\\frac{y-(3)}{12} \\\\ (12)(x-(-1)) & =(-8)(y-(3)) \\\\ (3)(x-(-1)) & =(-2)(y-(3)) \\\\ 3 x + 3 & =6 - 2 y \\\\ 3 x + 2 y - 3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["a3e69355-4465-5521-9779-bce1af127a1b"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "03eb4c04-9267-59ba-b869-c90be23347ec" :answer/id #uuid "03eb4c04-9267-59ba-b869-c90be23347ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3 x - 8 y - 18=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "bc0db264-9ef6-5c62-ae91-dd6cc4a6e716" :answer/id #uuid "bc0db264-9ef6-5c62-ae91-dd6cc4a6e716" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3 x - 4 y=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "50911ebd-2e23-5084-9d41-757a96a08045" :answer/id #uuid "50911ebd-2e23-5084-9d41-757a96a08045" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4 x + 3 y + 17=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9de33a7f-b967-5eba-9785-13d2ae9d81f4" :answer/id #uuid "9de33a7f-b967-5eba-9785-13d2ae9d81f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3 x - 4 y + 6=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "359c18da-2dc4-518a-a5c0-cd5436006e5e" :answer/id #uuid "359c18da-2dc4-518a-a5c0-cd5436006e5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3 x - 4 y - 6=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "3b978872-a86e-5385-abda-6a0fbfd634ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b978872-a86e-5385-abda-6a0fbfd634ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["03eb4c04-9267-59ba-b869-c90be23347ec" "bc0db264-9ef6-5c62-ae91-dd6cc4a6e716" "50911ebd-2e23-5084-9d41-757a96a08045" "9de33a7f-b967-5eba-9785-13d2ae9d81f4" "359c18da-2dc4-518a-a5c0-cd5436006e5e"] :answer-field/correct "359c18da-2dc4-518a-a5c0-cd5436006e5e" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "3df7d364-776e-5dbb-9f2e-436f4e9fc804" :question/id #uuid "3df7d364-776e-5dbb-9f2e-436f4e9fc804" :question/problem "Consider the plane curve $2 x^{2} + y^{2}=17.$  Find the equation of the normal line to the curve at the point $(-2,-3).$" :question/worked-solution "If we set $f(x,y)=2 x^{2} + y^{2}$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=17.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(-2,-3)$ can be found by computing $∇f(-2,-3).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(-2,-3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 x^{2} + y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2 x^{2} + y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(4 x)\\,i+(2 y)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(-2,-3) & =(4 (-2))\\,i+(2 (-3))\\,j \\\\  & =(-8)\\,i+(-6)\\,j \\\\  & =⟨-8,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(-2,-3)=⟨-8,-6⟩$ is a normal vector to the curve at $(-2,-3).$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}} & =\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}} \\\\ \\frac{x-(-2)}{-8} & =\\frac{y-(-3)}{-6} \\\\ (-6)(x-(-2)) & =(-8)(y-(-3)) \\\\ (-3)(x-(-2)) & =(-4)(y-(-3)) \\\\ - 3 x - 6 & =- 4 y - 12 \\\\ 3 x - 4 y - 6 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["3b978872-a86e-5385-abda-6a0fbfd634ee"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "f04fc7c8-e4a1-58fb-9dcc-daf30680e84a" :answer/id #uuid "f04fc7c8-e4a1-58fb-9dcc-daf30680e84a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x + 3 y - 6=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "330917b2-cba0-53ab-910e-6eea81df6b75" :answer/id #uuid "330917b2-cba0-53ab-910e-6eea81df6b75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x + 3 y + 6=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5c6fd1dd-a919-51be-b894-113cc9ed93f2" :answer/id #uuid "5c6fd1dd-a919-51be-b894-113cc9ed93f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x + 3 y=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fb695a72-da41-5585-8fc0-51f517403af8" :answer/id #uuid "fb695a72-da41-5585-8fc0-51f517403af8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x + 6 y + 15=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b2cb4d5b-4b25-55eb-9856-78437bedb5e1" :answer/id #uuid "b2cb4d5b-4b25-55eb-9856-78437bedb5e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3 x - y - 12=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "031f356f-2821-5db9-9c7a-f7890bd14e91" :answer-field/id #uuid "031f356f-2821-5db9-9c7a-f7890bd14e91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["f04fc7c8-e4a1-58fb-9dcc-daf30680e84a" "330917b2-cba0-53ab-910e-6eea81df6b75" "5c6fd1dd-a919-51be-b894-113cc9ed93f2" "fb695a72-da41-5585-8fc0-51f517403af8" "b2cb4d5b-4b25-55eb-9856-78437bedb5e1"] :answer-field/correct "330917b2-cba0-53ab-910e-6eea81df6b75" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "a06355a9-e2d0-5a7e-bed1-e1b39de7ef4e" :question/id #uuid "a06355a9-e2d0-5a7e-bed1-e1b39de7ef4e" :question/problem "Consider the plane curve $3 x^{2} + y^{2}=36.$  Find the equation of the normal line to the curve at the point $(3,-3).$" :question/worked-solution "If we set $f(x,y)=3 x^{2} + y^{2}$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=36.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(3,-3)$ can be found by computing $∇f(3,-3).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(3,-3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 x^{2} + y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 x^{2} + y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(6 x)\\,i+(2 y)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(3,-3) & =(6 (3))\\,i+(2 (-3))\\,j \\\\  & =(18)\\,i+(-6)\\,j \\\\  & =⟨18,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(3,-3)=⟨18,-6⟩$ is a normal vector to the curve at $(3,-3).$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}} & =\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}} \\\\ \\frac{x-(3)}{18} & =\\frac{y-(-3)}{-6} \\\\ (-6)(x-(3)) & =(18)(y-(-3)) \\\\ (-1)(x-(3)) & =(3)(y-(-3)) \\\\ 3 - x & =3 y + 9 \\\\ x + 3 y + 6 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["031f356f-2821-5db9-9c7a-f7890bd14e91"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "23d11206-9bb2-5dc4-b264-7e984cd3988a" :answer/id #uuid "23d11206-9bb2-5dc4-b264-7e984cd3988a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4 x + 3 y + 1=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2fac1bf6-c07f-518f-9bf8-a2eae2be9292" :answer/id #uuid "2fac1bf6-c07f-518f-9bf8-a2eae2be9292" :answer/type :answer.type/math